Rust crates
-----------

The Rust static library links 195 third-party crates from crates.io, each
under its own license as declared in its package metadata. Summary of the
declared license expressions (as reported by cargo on 2026-09-28):

  127  MIT OR Apache-2.0 (any spelling/order)
   29  MIT
   18  Unicode-3.0
    4  Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT
    2  Unlicense OR MIT
    2  MPL-2.0 (option-ext, webpki-roots)
    2  ISC
    2  Apache-2.0
    2  BSD-2-Clause OR MIT OR Apache-2.0
    1  Zlib
    1  BSD-3-Clause
    1  Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception OR Apache-2.0 OR MIT
    1  Apache-2.0 OR BSL-1.0
    1  Apache-2.0 AND ISC
    1  (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND Unicode-3.0
    1  (Apache-2.0 OR MIT) AND BSD-3-Clause

The MPL-2.0 crates are used unmodified; their source is available from
crates.io. Run `cargo tree -e normal --format '{p} {l}'` in rust/ostmac-core
for the full per-crate list.
